  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "| | Contables (plural) | Incontables |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| Preguntar | **How many** apples? | **How much** milk? |",
      "| Mucho/a | a lot of / **many** (en pregunta y negativa) | a lot of / **much** (en pregunta y negativa) |",
      "| Unos pocos | **a few** | **a little** |",
      "| Casi ninguno | **few** | **little** |",
      "| Demasiado | **too many** | **too much** |",
      "",
      "**Ojo:** en frases afirmativas se prefiere **a lot of**: *We've got a lot of crisps.* (no *much crisps*). *Much* y *many* se usan sobre todo en preguntas y negativas: *We haven't got much time. How many people are coming?*",
      "",
      "**a few / a little** = hay algunos (tono positivo). **few / little** (sin a) = casi no hay (tono negativo): *I've got a few friends here.* vs *I've got few friends here.*",
      "",
      "Pronunciación: *a few* /ə fjuː/ · *a little* /ə ˈlɪtl/."
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "How many water do you drink?",
        "right": "How much water do you drink?",
        "note": "Water es incontable."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "We have much people.",
        "right": "We have a lot of people.",
        "note": "Much casi no se usa en afirmativas."
      }
    ],
    "false_friends": []
  },
